{"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Sentence Stress", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class=\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\". ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Word stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">word</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Content Words</span> <ul><li> Content words are the important or key words of a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence.</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Structure Words </span>  <ul><li>Structure words are not important words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He started <span class = \"strong\">arguing </span>with the <span class = \"strong\">police officer.</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">What</span> a <span class = \"strong\">nightmare!</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should <span class = \"strong\"> see</span> the <span class = \"strong\">photos.</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class = \"strong\">Things</span> went from <span class = \"strong\"> bad</span> to  <span class = \"strong\">worse.</span>", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These words you use when you have problems.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sergeant ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an officer in a police force with a rank below captain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco had to get his driver's license from the sergeant in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to make it home", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to arrive home safely", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How did you make it home that night?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "all the way", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the entire distance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We had to walk all the way home.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "from bad to worse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a negative situation that does not improve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The evening went from bad to worse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to collect ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get things from different places", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He has to collect his license from the police station.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online and find 15 words that are spelled with the double <span class=\"italic\">ee</span>. Make a list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, create a 3-minute role play on what happened on Marco and Vanessa's date.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use at least 5 words that have a double <span class=\"italic\">ee</span> in the conversation.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can use the Internet to find new words to use in conversations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a 3-minute role play about a date.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I role play with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le12ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le12ob04re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le12ob04re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What happened after your phone died? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Things went from bad to worse.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: He started arguing with the police officer.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Really? Why?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: The police officer couldn't say his name properly. He kept calling him Mark or Markus.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "14400", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: He does have a strong accent and he was slurring ... right?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, it was embarrassing. I just looked down at my feet the whole time.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How did the night end?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: The officer took his driver's license and told him to collect it from the station in the morning.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le12ob04re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "29500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How did you get home?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: We had to w